{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqgzyyer7xl","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"Judge kickback: #13 phantom-node fix","summary":"Reviewed attempt branch orch/attempt/d42ebe37-ee9f-46b6-ae21-f6f82464d482-13. All 52 tests pass. Core nodeExistsInGraph guard is correct and well-tested. Two issues require a fix before merge:\n\n1. notifyChange(T.ws) regression (BLOCKING): The PR stripped T.ws from 13 notifyChange() calls in routes/overlay.js. In the base branch (main), every notifyChange() in overlay.js passes T.ws so SSE clients can filter by workspace (data: changed:<ws>). The attempt changed all of them to bare notifyChange() (data: changed). Impact: multi-workspace clients receive spurious cross-workspace refetch events. No updates are missed (bare events still fire for all clients), but this is a real regression introduced by the PR. The worker likely introduced this while inserting guard code and accidentally lost the T.ws arguments in the surrounding context. Fix: restore T.ws in all 13 calls in routes/overlay.js.\n\n2. /overlay/gate (create_gate) gap (SCOPE MISS): The handler takes blocking_task_key and calls overlayStore.addEdge(T.ov, key, b.blocking_task_key, null, 'blocking') without validating that b.blocking_task_key exists in the graph. This creates a phantom edge target — the exact bug class this PR was supposed to fix. Fix: add nodeExistsInGraph(buildGraph(T.ws), b.blocking_task_key) check before the addEdge call. Also add a test for this endpoint.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-16T18:50:27.123Z","vec":[-0.10052795708179474,-0.0016219989629462361,0.05520698428153992,0.05324742943048477,0.1525709480047226,-0.06325940787792206,0.02466617524623871,-0.01430624071508646,-0.0028827760834246874,0.04271493852138519,-0.005159273277968168,-0.006165481172502041,-0.016029268503189087,-0.06262268871068954,0.0076253945007920265,0.032006993889808655,0.03038923442363739,-0.037335556000471115,-0.06418080627918243,-0.04690072312951088,-0.05874273180961609,0.015